# Goal 10: Fix `ilogbf` zero return value

## Function
`ilogbf` (single-precision integer log base 2)

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/ilogbf.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s6/src/mathf.rs` (around line 1971, `ilogbf`)

## Problem
MISMATCH — 1 test failure. Same `FP_ILOGB0` bug as Goal 9.

```
C:    ilogbf 0.0f = -2147483647   (FP_ILOGB0)
Rust: ilogbf 0.0f = -2147483648   (INT_MIN)
```

## What Needs to Change
Use the correct `FP_ILOGB0` constant: `-2147483647` instead of `-2147483648`.

## Success Criteria
- `ilogbf(0.0f)` = `-2147483647` (bitwise match)
- All other `ilogbf` tests continue to pass
